== golang/go#54373 [closed/completed] created 2022-08-10 closed 2025-01-07 comments 2
x/tools/gopls: incorrect edits from the unused variable quickfix
Noticed this while preparing for the gopls@v0.9.2 release. The new unused variable quickfix added in #48975 seems to compute over-large edits in some cases. For example, given the following function: ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/57144380/183937614-85b6c8c6-eb29-4502-bec3-11cd9afa599c.png) The quick fix produces the following end-state: ![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/57144380/183937777-e771d24f-b441-4239-821a-027adf2dc614.png) I think this needs a bit more work before we enable this quick-fix by default. CC @rentziass for awareness. This is not a big deal, but I probably won't promote this new feature in the v0.9.2 release notes. We'll promote it for v0.10.0 once we've worked on it a bit more.

